+### git stale-branches
+
+Returns a list of local branches whose last commit is older than a date, oldest
+first, each with the date of that commit. This is the first step of a branch
+clean-up. The current branch and the main branch are never listed.
+
+    $ git stale-branches
+    2025-01-14	old-experiment
+    2025-03-02	feature/login
+
+The date defaults to 3 months ago, and can be specified using
+`git stale-branches -s <date>`, using any date format
+[supported by `git log`][gitlog]. A local branch is either "active" or "stale"
+for the same date (see `git active-branches`).
+
+Use `-m` to list only the stale branches that are merged into the main branch,
+or `-u` to list only the ones that are not:
+
+    $ git stale-branches -s 2025-02-01 -m
+    2025-01-14	old-experiment
+
